    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269-a2">

                <pb facs="0452" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 208.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Salisbury to
                        Mr. Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s note of the 26th ultimo, conveying the thanks
                    of the United States Government for the courtesy shown by Her Majesty’s
                    ambassador at Constantinople in authorizing the British vice-consul at Van to
                    take charge of American interests at that place.</p>
                <p>I am much gratified at this expression of thanks on the part of your excellency’s
                    Government, and I have not failed to acquaint Sir P. Currie with the terms of
                    your excellency’s note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
